{"kind":"report","text":"Discussed CLI JSON output from current parser, Outcome and acts/declaration sources. No JSON/format/output flag is currently accepted; acts flags list is empty, switches exclude json, and Outcome carries only code and lines. Proposed common --json with a versioned typed public result rendered as either text or JSON; merely serializing {code,lines} would preserve prose-parsing dependence. Default acts result retains full scope reference/incarnation, definition pin, caller key/member/standing, each independently read scope/membership head and role-filtered act catalog once. Each act keeps native step/on/grant and complete native field schemas (required, min/max, enums, nested record/list/item/ref types, defaults), plus nonempty also and presents/input requirements; do not flatten platform rule-mark forms. Omit guard/effect programs, sends/attention, unrelated live items and duplicate context from default; optional full-definition/detail view supplies native rule bodies. Catalog keyed by act kind as native definition.acts, not an array with duplicated kind fields. Native start/reset projection example demonstrates no artificial renaming to JSON Schema integer/action/targetType. Listing remains role-based, with rule-granted acts shown; guards not evaluated and native submission alone decides admission. Do not call them currently available acts or fabricate an availability boolean; finished Counter can still list Start. Source-only C1 measurement: 13 non-genesis full act definitions total8436 compact UTF-8 bytes; pick step/on/grant/fields/nonempty also totals2705 bytes; complete declaration12691 bytes, before result metadata. Retain IDs/hash values intact for machines. For the broader CLI, preserve native Read/Answer/Receipt/replay structures as appropriate, stable structured errors/exit codes and JSON-only stdout. Aggregated role/catalog reads are not an atomic native snapshot and require distinct heads. No source, flag, tests, live read, native act or output format was changed."}